<p>Mr. Draper’s parents came to North Dakota with him in 1881 and became members of Mandan's Episcopal Church. His father Valney returned to the mercantile business and operated a store in Mandan for several years. Draper's sister Olivia Mary (who would later refer to herself as Mary to avoid confusion with her niece Olivia) would marry to E. C.(Ezekiel) Rice, the attorney, who would also serve as Morton County States attorney.In 1900 Mr. Draper organized the Mandan Telephone Company. Mandan News August 1898 Ad</p>

